{{Short description|Administrative entry restrictions}}
[[File:Afghan Passport first issued in 2017.jpg|thumb|180px|[[Afghan passport]] (2017–present design)|upright=1.1]]

'''Visa requirements for Afghan citizens''' are administrative entry restrictions by the authorities of other states placed on citizens of [[Afghanistan]].

As of 2026, Afghan citizens had visa-free or visa on arrival access to only 24 countries and territories, ranking the [[Afghanistan passport]] 101st and worst in the world according to the [[Henley & Partners Passport Index|Henley Passport Index]].<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.henleyglobal.com/passport-index/ranking | title=Global Passport Ranking}}</ref>

Obtaining foreign visas from within Afghanistan is difficult as many [[List of diplomatic missions in Afghanistan|embassies in Afghanistan]] have closed since [[2021 Taliban offensive|Taliban takeover of the government in August 2021]].<ref>{{cite news | author1=Amy Cheng | author2=Haq Nawaz Khan | title=Hundreds of Afghans gather outside passport office as Taliban resumes issuing travel documents | url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2021/10/06/afghanistan-taliban-passport-refugee/ | access-date=9 December 2021 | newspaper=[[The Washington Post]] | date=6 October 2021}}</ref> Prices of Afghan passports have risen dramatically as a result of broken down bureaucracy and increased demand.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://kabulnow.com/2023/01/passports-how-taliban-officials-have-turned-the-worlds-weakest-into-the-most-expensive/|title=How Taliban officials have turned the world's weakest passports into the most expensive|publisher=KabulNow|date=25 January 2023|accessdate=24 January 2025}}</ref>

